                            <comment id="431305" author="yujian" created="Mon, 14 Oct 2024 04:56:40 +0000">&lt;p&gt;2.16.0 RC2: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c60de329-04c8-40fe-bac2-7b30d65f2ba0" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c60de329-04c8-40fe-bac2-7b30d65f2ba0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The failure occurred 48 times in the last 6 months.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="502740" author="adilger" created="Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:56:06 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;Claude&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; +17 (or more) failures in the past 6 months, failed 12/9627 runs in the past 4 weeks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/84ea04cd-700e-4a9b-8925-327210f8f0ab" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/84ea04cd-700e-4a9b-8925-327210f8f0ab&lt;/a&gt; (2026-08-31 lustre-master full-dne-part-2)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/8e69b7c8-684e-42e1-b68b-dc54554a6c9a" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/8e69b7c8-684e-42e1-b68b-dc54554a6c9a&lt;/a&gt; (2026-10-02 lustre-reviews review-dne-part-2)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="504086" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:45:56 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Rainshadow triage (2026-09-22 to 2026-10-21): 92 failed sessions, 60 on branch runs. All 60 branch failures are full-part-2 interop sessions (master client vs b2_15 or b2_16 servers, every client distro), and every failing build fails in all 12 configs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cause of the "lst Error found" ones (48 of 60): CI runs LNet with accept_port=7988. Before &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20770" title="interop sanity-pfl,sanityn: Request sent has failed due to network error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20770"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20770&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (change 69145, merged) master clients connected their bulk sockets to port 988, which 2.15/2.16 servers do not listen on. With only a control conn, zero-copy requests cannot be ACKed (-113), connections are reset, and lst shows brw errors and expired RPCs ("Total 2 error nodes in c/s"). Example: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c4820c6f-e1da-4524-b1ab-34d4c3a91657" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c4820c6f-e1da-4524-b1ab-34d4c3a91657&lt;/a&gt; (server brw_bulk_ready -113, client "Host reset our connection ... rc = -104"). Every one of these ran a master build older than &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20770" title="interop sanity-pfl,sanityn: Request sent has failed due to network error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20770"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20770&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (2.17.59_1, _52, _68, _78).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduced in ltvm (rocky8, b2_15 server, master client, accept_port=7988, lst smoke as in test_smoke with SLOW=no): master without &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20770" title="interop sanity-pfl,sanityn: Request sent has failed due to network error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20770"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20770&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fails 5/5; master tip with &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20770" title="interop sanity-pfl,sanityn: Request sent has failed due to network error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20770"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20770&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; passes 5/5.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The remaining 12 branch failures ("smoke.sh failed: 253", master-next 2026-10-14) are unrelated to this: unmerged change 67626 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20513" title="lnet_selftest failed on ARM with 'simple' check mode" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20513"&gt;LU-20513&lt;/a&gt;) adds LST_FEAT_BULK_STRIDE and old nodes reject the session with EPROTO (already noted on that change). That build did contain &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20770" title="interop sanity-pfl,sanityn: Request sent has failed due to network error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20770"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20770&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No new patch needed for the interop failures. Not explained: ~0.25% of lustre-reviews runs (mostly arm groups, a few x86) and the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16876" title="lnet-selftest test_smoke: timeout (&amp;quot;2 batch in stopping&amp;quot;)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16876"&gt;LU-16876&lt;/a&gt; timeouts, a different mode with ping errors and no -113.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
